9. Conclusion
ArrayList is an appropriate engineering choice for normal music playlists because it provides fast random access, efficient iteration and fast insertion at the end.

LinkedList is more suitable when frequent insertions and deletions are performed at the beginning or when an iterator is already positioned at the required location.

However, when the application introduces an Up Next queue with frequent additions at both ends and removals from the front, ArrayDeque becomes the better choice.

Therefore, the best data structure depends on the operations performed most frequently by the application.
